## --- global (local) ---

## General Guidelines
- Write concise, readable, and self-documenting code.
- Prefer explicit over implicit implementations.
- Write tests for any complex logic.

## Git Conventions
- Use semantic commit messages (e.g., `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`).
- Keep commits small and focused.


