## --- agent-skills-osmani (local) ---

## Addy Osmani's Agent Skills — Production-Grade Engineering Workflows
> Source: https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills
> Install (Antigravity): `agy plugin install https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills.git`
> Install (Claude Code): `/plugin marketplace add addyosmani/agent-skills`
> Install (Cursor): Copy `SKILL.md` files into `.cursor/rules/`

24 production-grade engineering skills for AI coding agents, organized around the full development lifecycle: Define → Plan → Build → Verify → Review → Ship.

### Lifecycle Commands
| Phase | Command | Key Principle |
|-------|---------|---------------|
| Define what to build | `/spec` | Spec before code |
| Plan how to build it | `/plan` | Small, atomic tasks |
| Build incrementally | `/build` | One slice at a time |
| Prove it works | `/test` | Tests are proof |
| Review before merge | `/review` | Improve code health |
| Simplify the code | `/code-simplify` | Clarity over cleverness |
| Ship to production | `/ship` | Faster is safer |

### Skill Categories
- **Meta**: `using-agent-skills` — maps incoming work to the right skill workflow
- **Define**: `interview-me`, `idea-refine`, `spec-driven-development`
- **Plan**: Task decomposition and implementation planning
- **Build**: `frontend-ui-engineering`, `api-and-interface-design`, incremental implementation
- **Verify**: Test-driven verification and debugging
- **Review**: Code review quality gates
- **Ship**: Production deployment workflows

### Key Features
- `/build auto` — generates plan and implements every task in a single approved pass.
- Skills activate automatically based on context (e.g., designing an API triggers `api-and-interface-design`).
- Works with Claude Code, Cursor, Antigravity, Gemini CLI, Windsurf, OpenCode, GitHub Copilot, Codex, and more.
- Each skill is a structured workflow with steps, verification gates, and anti-rationalization tables.
